# reel's hero demo: reel recording a demo of itself. Three tracks at once: a terminal that records musicbox.reel, a
# code screen that follows that reel's script as it runs, and Musicbox, attached once the reel in the terminal opens
# it, with its own sound. The director moves between them and narrates over the whole.
# `mise run demos showcase` records it (Musicbox built in ~/Projects/musicbox, its drawer closed:
# `defaults write dev.musicbox.app drawerOpen -bool false`). It plays music and takes the mouse and keyboard.
Import //demos/reel.reelpreset

Screen terminal as term
  Set WorkingDirectory //demos
  Set Columns 72
  Set Rows 12
  Set FontSize 18
  Set Title "demos — zsh"
  Set WaitTimeout 3m
  Type@0ms "export PATH=$PWD/../.build/debug:$PATH; clear"
  Key return
  Wait exit as ready
  Wait for hello to end
  Type "reel record musicbox.reel"
  Key return as run
  Wait /take: / as recorded
  Wait exit
  Wait for rendering
  Type "reel render musicbox.reel --profile github"
  Key return
  Wait /wrote .*musicbox-github.gif/ as rendered
  Wait exit

Screen code as script
  Set Viewport 900x560
  Set FontSize 16
  Set WaitTimeout 3m
  Code musicbox.reel
  Follow
  Wait for recorded to end

Attach ~/Projects/musicbox/build/App/Musicbox.app as app

Output //docs/media/showcase.mp4
Output //docs/media/showcase.gif
# The terminal and its script side by side; stacked beside Musicbox once it opens.
Set Layout term | script
# A second voice, as musicbox.reel has.
Set Voice guest voicebox:Michael
# The take in the terminal runs for minutes: every wait for it waits as long.
Set WaitTimeout 3m
Intro@crossfade,ease-out,600ms square ? "reel" "Demo videos from a script" : 2s
Outro@fade,800ms square ? "Recorded with reel" "brew install --cask mpdreamz/tap/reel" : 2s

Hide
Wait for ready
Show
Say "Reel turns a plain text script into a finished demo video. To show how, it's recording a demo of itself." as hello
Wait for run
Say "A terminal runs one reel, while a code screen beneath it follows that reel's script, line by line."
Wait for app
Layout@smooth,1s (term / script) | app
Say "Musicbox, a macOS app we record for this demo, sound and all."
Spotlight@smooth,1s app
Say "Every click, key press and zoom it receives comes from a single line of that script."
Pip@smooth,1s script over app top-left
# The reel in the terminal is silent while it records: its own lines are voiced when it renders.
Say "The narration in that script stays silent while recording. Reel voices it, and mixes it in, during the render."
# Musicbox's steps are named in musicbox.reel: the director speaks as each one happens.
Wait for play
Say "A press of the space bar starts the music."
# Musicbox's clicks wait for these markers (Wait for muting, unmuting): each lands on its word.
Say@guest,over "Reel finds the drums' mute button by its accessibility name, and [mute] clicks it."
Wait [mute] as muting
Wait for back to end
Say@guest,over "Clicking it [unmute] again, the beat is unmuted!"
Wait [unmute] as unmuting
# recorded and rendered are Waits, which start as soon as they wait: these wait for them to end.
Wait for recorded to end
Pip off
Layout@smooth,1s (term / script) | app
Say "Once the take is done, reel renders it: voices, subtitles and zooms, with a cut for every place the video will go." as rendering
Say "A render may take a few minutes in real time, so let's skip ahead."
# The render shows nothing new until it writes: cut to its end.
Hide
Wait for rendered to end
Show
Say@guest "Mac apps, web pages, terminals and code walkthroughs, recorded together and directed from one script."
Say "Write it once, and let reel do the takes. Have fun with it!"
Sleep 1s
